{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Plan revised again after 2nd review-plan BLOCK (1 finding, G6): the recovery 'single shared cached segment' was physically unrealizable — recovery builds independent per-criterion RunRequests with no shared history (only system_prompt/instructions/cache_prefix). Corrected: the recovery prefetch is a BYTE-STABLE block at a fixed system_prompt position via cache_prefix, so it is cache-READ across the N per-criterion runs (that is the economy, not a single physical copy — the opposite arm from the primary verifier's message-tail cache, because recovery has no shared message history). Bytes still counted against physical_context_ceiling."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786085243575623001,"uuid":"b57dfbe9-963f-4898-bd39-8c94058c9d5c"}